<Layout title="Privacy" description="How newsletter subscriptions and reader messages are handled on PublicDomainPulp.net."><header class="page-intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Reader information</p><h1>Privacy.</h1></header><article class="editorial wrap"><p>This page describes the website’s current features. Questions can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p><h2>Newsletter subscriptions</h2><p>Newsletter signup is provided by Substack, including forms embedded in this website. Substack receives the information you enter in its form and handles subscription management. Its form links to its terms, privacy policy, and information collection notice. Visiting an embedded form also connects your browser to Substack.</p><p><a href="https://substack.com/privacy">Read Substack’s privacy policy ↗</a></p><h2>Reader messages</h2>{feedbackMode==='email'?<p>The contact form prepares a draft in your email app. The website does not store your draft. If you send it, the name, reply address and message you include are delivered to the publisher’s email inbox and handled by the email services involved.</p>:<p>The contact form sends your name, email address and message through the hosting provider’s form service so the publisher can respond. Do not include passwords or sensitive personal information in reader feedback.</p>}<p>Sending a message does not subscribe you to the newsletter. Contact the publisher if you want to ask about a message you have sent.</p><h2>Other services</h2><p>Book links open Amazon. The companion playlist opens Spotify. Those services apply their own policies when you visit them. The site does not contain advertising trackers or a separate analytics script in this build. The hosting provider may process ordinary connection and access logs to serve the website.</p><h2>Updates</h2><p>This information will be updated if the website’s forms or services change. Last updated October 17, 2026.</p></article></Layout>
